WEBVTT

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:23.780
<i>Every day I keep wondering if</i>
<i>there's something missing.</i>

00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:31.120
<i>I still want to keep feeling my</i>
<i>heart beating in anticipation.</i>

00:00:31.190 --> 00:00:38.850
<i>Ideals are far out of reach, but</i>
<i>reality is within my grasp.</i>

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:45.000
<i>It's not easy standing against the wind,</i>
<i>but as long as I keep smiling...</i>

00:00:45.100 --> 00:00:49.770
<i>... staying true to myself,</i>
<i>I'll become stronger.</i>

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:57.480
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll find him and take my chance.</i>

00:00:57.550 --> 00:01:04.450
<i>I'll make the whole world stop</i>
<i>to see the angel that I'll be.</i>

00:01:04.520 --> 00:01:12.390
<i>I know I'll love somebody. Someday</i>
<i>I'll meet the man of my dreams.</i>

00:01:12.490 --> 00:01:20.060
<i>Nothing can slow me down. Tomorrow</i>
<i>is just around the corner.</i>

00:01:38.290 --> 00:01:39.660
Hurry, mom!

00:01:39.660 --> 00:01:41.620
Okay, okay.

00:01:53.270 --> 00:01:56.170
Aah! I love
shopping!

00:01:56.270 --> 00:01:59.730
Feels like ages since I've gone
out and spent some money!

00:01:59.910 --> 00:02:01.380
What are you talking
about?

00:02:01.480 --> 00:02:03.980
Who just changed her brake pads?!

00:02:03.980 --> 00:02:06.040
That doesn't count.

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:10.020
Shopping means fashion,
Miyuki. Fashion!

00:02:10.290 --> 00:02:12.580
Hey, that reminds
me. I'm starving.

00:02:12.690 --> 00:02:14.260
What do you want to do for dinner?

00:02:14.260 --> 00:02:16.160
Dinner?! We just ate!

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:17.650
Yeah, yeah.

00:02:17.760 --> 00:02:20.020
Listen, there's a place I've
been wanting to go to.

00:02:27.900 --> 00:02:29.370
Here it is!

00:02:29.370 --> 00:02:31.030
This place?

00:02:31.610 --> 00:02:35.240
But this is that department
store that just opened.

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:41.010
Precisely. I heard there's a really nice
restaurant up on the 12th floor.

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:48.520
Ooh, isn't that cute!
Look, Natsumi.

00:02:48.690 --> 00:02:49.820
I'm looking.

00:02:54.560 --> 00:02:55.660
You know...

00:02:55.760 --> 00:02:58.860
...they're running a huge
sale on formal dresses.

00:02:59.300 --> 00:03:01.570
Yeah, but where would you wear it?

00:03:01.570 --> 00:03:05.540
It's okay to occasionally get gussied up.

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:06.910
Don't be silly.

00:03:06.910 --> 00:03:08.880
I'm not. Let's check it out.

00:03:10.610 --> 00:03:16.110
You've reached Marukoshi Department
store, here to serve your every need.

00:03:16.220 --> 00:03:18.580
Pardon? What
did you say?

00:03:18.690 --> 00:03:20.280
A bomb?

00:03:20.520 --> 00:03:25.430
FILE. 30
FOREVER MY
BELOVED RIKO

00:03:33.240 --> 00:03:35.470
What are you doing
with all of those?!

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:38.770
Doesn't cost a thing
to try them on!

00:03:39.340 --> 00:03:42.240
Don't just stand
there...

00:03:42.340 --> 00:03:44.070
...you've got to be whimsical
once in a while.

00:03:44.250 --> 00:03:45.710
Whimsical?

00:03:46.150 --> 00:03:47.740
Get with it!

00:03:47.850 --> 00:03:52.410
You've got to put on something like this
now and then to get Nakajima fired up!

00:03:54.560 --> 00:03:56.520
What, this?

00:04:01.930 --> 00:04:04.360
Well, maybe not that,
but something sexy!

00:04:04.530 --> 00:04:06.700
Maybe I will try it on.

00:04:06.700 --> 00:04:07.830
Huh?

00:04:07.940 --> 00:04:09.270
Yeah. Sure.

00:04:09.370 --> 00:04:13.670
Good idea. Well, on to
the changing room!

00:04:13.840 --> 00:04:15.780
Excuse me.

00:04:15.940 --> 00:04:16.740
Huh?!

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:20.440
These are absolutely delicious,
ma'am. I guarantee it!

00:04:23.450 --> 00:04:25.420
What?! I don't
believe it!

00:04:26.960 --> 00:04:29.820
Ladies and Gentlemen, this is
an important announcement.

00:04:29.930 --> 00:04:32.860
We have just received
a suspicious call...

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:37.020
...and must ask you to leave the store
as a precautionary measure.

00:04:37.330 --> 00:04:42.200
To repeat, we ask that you leave
the store quickly, but with care.

00:04:42.300 --> 00:04:45.300
Follow the directions of the staff
and leave the store at once.

00:04:45.410 --> 00:04:48.380
If you notice any suspicious packages,
please do not touch them.

00:04:48.480 --> 00:04:50.710
Again, please do not touch
any suspicious packages.

00:04:50.810 --> 00:04:53.080
Please proceed directly
to the nearest exit.

00:04:55.420 --> 00:04:58.980
I just want you to know that I'm
not doing this for Nakajima.

00:04:59.150 --> 00:05:00.520
Yeah, yeah.

00:05:00.520 --> 00:05:02.590
Yeah, yeah.
I'm just trying it on, that's all.

00:05:02.590 --> 00:05:02.720
I'm just trying it on, that's all.

00:05:02.720 --> 00:05:03.560
Yeah, yeah.

00:05:03.560 --> 00:05:04.760
Not "yeah, yeah!" Yes!

00:05:04.760 --> 00:05:05.850
Yes!

00:05:07.730 --> 00:05:11.930
But seriously, I wonder what
kind of style he likes?

00:05:12.100 --> 00:05:15.540
H... How would I know
what Nakajima likes?

00:05:16.370 --> 00:05:22.470
Who says I was talking
about Nakajima?

00:05:22.640 --> 00:05:24.870
Natsumi! Oh!

00:05:25.050 --> 00:05:26.380
What the heck's going on?

00:05:36.530 --> 00:05:39.760
I read about something like
this in a book once.

00:05:39.930 --> 00:05:40.900
Yeah?

00:05:41.060 --> 00:05:44.260
It was aboard the Marie
Celeste, in 1872.

00:05:44.370 --> 00:05:48.800
All of the ship's passengers suddenly
disappeared, never to be seen again.

00:05:49.040 --> 00:05:53.000
Don't tell me any more! I hate
those kinds of stories!

00:05:53.180 --> 00:05:54.040
Come on.

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:54.640
Uh...

00:05:54.640 --> 00:05:57.050
We've got to find out what's going on first!

00:05:57.050 --> 00:05:59.010
Wait for me! Ow!

00:06:06.560 --> 00:06:08.320
What're we going
to do?

00:06:08.490 --> 00:06:11.480
I don't know yet. But, first, let's
look around the store.

00:06:11.660 --> 00:06:14.720
Gotcha. Let's
split up!

00:06:19.370 --> 00:06:20.060
Natsumi?!

00:06:23.510 --> 00:06:25.130
Hmm? Tsujimoto?!

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:27.580
What are you
doing here?

00:06:29.650 --> 00:06:31.140
Natsumi!

00:06:31.310 --> 00:06:33.280
Detective Tokuno!

00:06:33.920 --> 00:06:34.610
A bomb?!

00:06:34.780 --> 00:06:35.810
Mm-hmm.

00:06:35.980 --> 00:06:37.180
Uh-huh.

00:06:37.290 --> 00:06:40.280
Now, what were you saying
about that boat?

00:06:40.460 --> 00:06:43.290
Shh! There's no need
to bring that up now.

00:06:43.390 --> 00:06:46.760
Anyway! Detective, Natsumi and I
would be more than glad to help.

00:06:46.930 --> 00:06:48.900
Thanks. We'll
need you.

00:06:49.500 --> 00:06:54.700
What'll happen to the sale?! The sale!
Today's the last day of the big sale!

00:06:54.870 --> 00:06:57.340
Well, ma'am, at this point I can't...

00:06:57.340 --> 00:06:58.530
Stop right there.

00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:02.040
How about the spring collection sale and
the gourmet fair in the food court?

00:07:02.210 --> 00:07:02.310
First of all, you can look after that.

00:07:02.310 --> 00:07:04.650
What about the special gourmet pickle fair?

00:07:04.650 --> 00:07:06.310
Great.

00:07:06.580 --> 00:07:09.070
What do you think
you're doing?

00:07:09.180 --> 00:07:12.210
How dare you treat a good
customer like that!

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:13.850
I won't give
up!

00:07:13.960 --> 00:07:17.430
I'm staying here until I get an explanation!

00:07:17.430 --> 00:07:20.190
Listen ma'am, I'm telling you...

00:07:23.670 --> 00:07:28.360
Uh... I'll
get it.

00:07:28.470 --> 00:07:30.170
You've reached Marukoshi Department...

00:07:30.170 --> 00:07:32.240
Enough with the greeting.

00:07:32.240 --> 00:07:33.760
It's you!

00:07:33.880 --> 00:07:36.840
What on Earth do
you think...

00:07:38.550 --> 00:07:40.980
What do you want
from us?

00:07:41.950 --> 00:07:43.850
Hmph. Nothing
special.

00:07:43.950 --> 00:07:46.980
I just don't like your
store, that's all.

00:07:47.660 --> 00:07:49.620
That's ridiculous.

00:07:51.730 --> 00:07:54.490
How about I give
you a little hint?

00:07:54.730 --> 00:07:56.670
Are you listening? It's Riko!

00:07:56.670 --> 00:07:58.060
Are you listening? It's Riko!
Huh?

00:07:58.230 --> 00:08:00.130
Could you
trace it?

00:08:03.070 --> 00:08:05.040
It's Riko!

00:08:06.340 --> 00:08:09.740
All right. Find
this Riko!

00:08:17.220 --> 00:08:19.190
Any luck,
Miyuki?

00:08:21.990 --> 00:08:25.320
Not even close. No Rieko, no
Rikako, Risako or Ritsuko!

00:08:25.430 --> 00:08:28.490
It'll take hours to go through
all the files!

00:08:30.600 --> 00:08:32.360
Detective Tokuno. What time is
the bomb going to explode?

00:08:32.530 --> 00:08:33.760
At six.

00:08:33.940 --> 00:08:34.990
Huh?!

00:08:35.100 --> 00:08:38.070
It's already 5;20! We've only
got 40 minutes left.

00:08:38.240 --> 00:08:41.330
We'll just have to
search for it.

00:08:41.440 --> 00:08:44.340
Detective, please give us as
much support as you can.

00:08:44.450 --> 00:08:45.880
Let's go, Natsumi.

00:09:06.400 --> 00:09:09.230
No stores named
Riko, either.

00:09:09.400 --> 00:09:15.040
If only there was someone who knew
everything about this store!

00:09:15.210 --> 00:09:16.950
Even more than the manager?

00:09:16.950 --> 00:09:17.650
Huh?

00:09:17.650 --> 00:09:18.480
Oh.

00:09:18.650 --> 00:09:19.510
There is someone!
There is someone!

00:09:20.680 --> 00:09:23.480
I know her!

00:09:24.290 --> 00:09:25.320
Who is she?

00:09:25.320 --> 00:09:26.840
Where is she?

00:09:27.020 --> 00:09:28.190
I don't know.

00:09:28.190 --> 00:09:29.450
How do we find her?!

00:09:30.060 --> 00:09:32.320
I don't know where
Riko is right now.

00:09:32.430 --> 00:09:34.260
Riko is...

00:09:34.360 --> 00:09:38.990
Riko is a doll. The one that
used to be in the clock.

00:09:39.170 --> 00:09:40.230
That's right!

00:09:50.180 --> 00:09:52.480
Where is that
doll?

00:09:52.650 --> 00:09:54.950
Now, let me
see...

00:09:58.990 --> 00:10:03.420
Riko was an icon at our store
about five years ago.

00:10:03.530 --> 00:10:05.190
She was popular
and all...

00:10:05.290 --> 00:10:07.320
But the clock
was old...

00:10:07.430 --> 00:10:12.870
...so last month we replaced
it with something newer.

00:10:12.970 --> 00:10:16.030
So we took the old
doll and we...

00:10:16.200 --> 00:10:19.200
I've got it! This looks
like the box!

00:10:19.710 --> 00:10:22.070
Let's go!

00:10:24.310 --> 00:10:26.610
Careful. Careful.

00:10:36.120 --> 00:10:39.460
Stand back. We'll
defuse it.

00:10:39.630 --> 00:10:40.820
Be careful.

00:10:58.110 --> 00:10:59.080
Detective!

00:10:59.180 --> 00:11:03.380
We've defused the bomb. We will
be removing it immediately.

00:11:03.550 --> 00:11:05.210
Good. Nice
work.

00:11:06.820 --> 00:11:11.550
5;30. That was
a close call.

00:11:12.560 --> 00:11:13.500
Miyuki?

00:11:13.500 --> 00:11:15.690
Miyuki?
That was too simple.

00:11:15.800 --> 00:11:19.700
Why would the guy put
a bomb in here?

00:11:20.340 --> 00:11:21.200
Hmm?

00:11:21.300 --> 00:11:25.210
Well, let's leave that to Detective
Tokuno to figure out.

00:11:25.510 --> 00:11:26.630
It doesn't make
sense.

00:11:26.740 --> 00:11:29.870
Usually bombs are in much
more conspicuous places.

00:11:29.980 --> 00:11:32.570
Why would it be in
a warehouse?

00:11:32.680 --> 00:11:34.770
Tied to an abandoned
doll?

00:11:35.320 --> 00:11:36.550
Now that you
mention it...

00:11:36.650 --> 00:11:39.280
...that hint he gave us
was pretty obvious.

00:11:39.520 --> 00:11:42.790
It was almost like he
wanted us to find it.

00:11:43.560 --> 00:11:44.790
Wait a second!

00:11:45.460 --> 00:11:47.220
What are you
doing?

00:11:49.930 --> 00:11:52.870
I knew it! It's
a fake!

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:06.070
Even if it did blow, it wouldn't
have amounted to much.

00:12:06.750 --> 00:12:09.240
I know, maybe it was
all just a big joke.

00:12:09.420 --> 00:12:11.190
It's too involved to just be a joke.

00:12:11.190 --> 00:12:12.020
Oh, yeah.

00:12:12.790 --> 00:12:13.850
No leads...

00:12:14.020 --> 00:12:15.990
Oh, no. Don't
say that.

00:12:20.560 --> 00:12:21.530
It's me.

00:12:21.700 --> 00:12:23.100
Y... You!

00:12:24.330 --> 00:12:26.960
Recognize me,
do you?

00:12:27.070 --> 00:12:29.160
So tell me, did you
find the bomb?

00:12:30.010 --> 00:12:32.940
You tricked us!
It was a fake!

00:12:33.110 --> 00:12:34.080
My!

00:12:34.180 --> 00:12:37.240
You've done well. Keep
up the good work...

00:12:37.350 --> 00:12:39.010
...and you'll find
the real thing.

00:12:39.580 --> 00:12:41.070
How dare
you!

00:12:41.180 --> 00:12:43.980
Why are you doing
this to us?

00:12:44.890 --> 00:12:46.850
Listen up.

00:12:49.020 --> 00:12:52.980
Young man! How long are you
planning to stay in there?!

00:12:53.430 --> 00:12:54.690
Other people are waiting
to use the phone!

00:12:54.800 --> 00:12:57.320
Now hang up and
run along.

00:12:57.430 --> 00:12:58.760
That voice...
Why don't you move away.

00:12:58.930 --> 00:13:01.040
It can only be one person.
Young people, they're so inconsiderate!

00:13:01.040 --> 00:13:03.000
Let's go!

00:13:08.110 --> 00:13:08.940
Over there!

00:13:09.440 --> 00:13:10.670
Would you please hang up?

00:13:11.280 --> 00:13:15.110
Leave me alone, you old hag.

00:13:15.280 --> 00:13:16.980
Stop right there!
Look at my nice and silky skin.

00:13:17.090 --> 00:13:18.550
I'm using a special product.

00:13:18.790 --> 00:13:20.060
That's why my skin is so nice.

00:13:20.060 --> 00:13:21.780
Let go!

00:13:24.230 --> 00:13:26.190
Stop!

00:13:41.980 --> 00:13:42.910
Outta my
way!

00:13:51.320 --> 00:13:53.220
Detective Tokuno!

00:13:57.060 --> 00:13:58.030
Got him!

00:13:58.390 --> 00:14:00.450
D... Damn you! Itadaki!?

00:14:01.100 --> 00:14:03.200
Why you...

00:14:03.200 --> 00:14:04.030
All right, all right.

00:14:06.400 --> 00:14:07.490
Mr. Itadaki.

00:14:07.600 --> 00:14:11.370
You are the one who made
Riko, aren't you?

00:14:13.310 --> 00:14:15.370
But why'd you
do it?

00:14:15.540 --> 00:14:18.480
Because they took
Riko away.

00:14:19.010 --> 00:14:23.140
Riko was my master-
piece.

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:25.950
And they replaced it with
that piece of crap.

00:14:26.290 --> 00:14:27.520
I don't know...

00:14:27.620 --> 00:14:29.660
...I kind of like the new one.

00:14:29.660 --> 00:14:33.820
You fool! Don't compare my Riko to that!

00:14:34.260 --> 00:14:36.060
Whatever, it's just a doll, after all.

00:14:36.060 --> 00:14:37.960
No!

00:14:38.070 --> 00:14:41.040
Riko's much more than a doll
to me. More than a person!

00:14:41.670 --> 00:14:44.870
And to think she was replaced
with that... that thing!

00:14:45.040 --> 00:14:46.560
Mr. Itadaki...

00:14:47.110 --> 00:14:49.940
The real bomb's
in the clock...

00:14:50.040 --> 00:14:51.670
...isn't it?

00:14:51.850 --> 00:14:53.750
How did
you...

00:14:56.080 --> 00:14:57.350
Come on,
Natsumi!

00:14:57.520 --> 00:14:59.490
Yeah!

00:15:02.260 --> 00:15:05.120
<i>Ten to six! We've</i>
<i>got to hurry!</i>

00:15:05.290 --> 00:15:06.760
Miyuki!

00:15:06.860 --> 00:15:08.490
How did you
know?!

00:15:08.660 --> 00:15:11.790
He loved
Riko!

00:15:11.970 --> 00:15:16.060
So he couldn't forgive the other
dolls for replacing her!

00:15:17.370 --> 00:15:19.030
In here!

00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:26.350
I don't believe it!

00:15:26.350 --> 00:15:28.820
It's welded shut!

00:15:28.980 --> 00:15:30.970
Here goes!

00:15:41.530 --> 00:15:44.360
Here. Let
me try.

00:15:47.670 --> 00:15:49.530
Wait... my merchandise!

00:15:49.940 --> 00:15:50.700
Pardon?

00:15:50.870 --> 00:15:52.400
Uh... nothing.

00:15:58.680 --> 00:16:02.310
Oh, my precious
merchandise.

00:16:03.850 --> 00:16:07.310
That's good, Miyuki. I
can take it from here.

00:16:17.230 --> 00:16:20.900
What the heck
has he done?

00:16:21.070 --> 00:16:23.200
Look! Over
there!

00:16:27.010 --> 00:16:28.440
So that's where he put the bomb.

00:16:28.440 --> 00:16:31.210
And that's why we only have until 6;00!

00:16:31.380 --> 00:16:32.900
Detective Tokuno!

00:16:33.680 --> 00:16:34.280
Where's the bomb?

00:16:34.280 --> 00:16:35.420
In here! Take care of it!

00:16:35.420 --> 00:16:37.480
Yes, sir!

00:16:51.870 --> 00:16:53.030
This is no
good.

00:16:53.130 --> 00:16:55.070
At this rate, it'll take
a gazillion years!

00:16:55.800 --> 00:16:57.340
What can we do?

00:16:57.340 --> 00:17:00.100
They say, "If you can't push, try pulling!"

00:17:00.910 --> 00:17:01.640
What?

00:17:01.640 --> 00:17:04.610
It'd be easier to work from the outside.

00:17:13.560 --> 00:17:14.950
What are you
going to do?

00:17:15.120 --> 00:17:17.680
Natsumi! Will
this stuff do?

00:17:18.260 --> 00:17:20.800
Yeah, I guess it'll have to.

00:17:20.800 --> 00:17:23.090
Oh... my merchandise!

00:17:30.640 --> 00:17:31.510
Where's the rope?

00:17:31.510 --> 00:17:32.440
Got it.

00:17:35.540 --> 00:17:36.980
These clothes'll get in the way.

00:17:36.980 --> 00:17:38.410
I agree.

00:17:40.580 --> 00:17:43.310
Excuse me, but that's
my merchandise...

00:17:44.150 --> 00:17:46.280
Ready?

00:17:47.120 --> 00:17:49.490
Tsujimoto... Kobayakawa...

00:18:00.740 --> 00:18:03.360
Hey! Quit
peeking!

00:18:08.110 --> 00:18:10.040
Crazy...

00:18:15.420 --> 00:18:18.280
Ready?

00:18:32.630 --> 00:18:34.970
Look out
below!

00:18:38.240 --> 00:18:39.760
I can't take this
anymore.

00:18:39.940 --> 00:18:41.380
How much time do we have?

00:18:41.380 --> 00:18:43.340
Three minutes.

00:18:50.490 --> 00:18:51.920
Think you can do something?

00:18:51.920 --> 00:18:52.780
Yeah!

00:18:58.030 --> 00:19:00.760
Come on,
you two.

00:19:03.770 --> 00:19:05.530
Pliers.

00:19:05.630 --> 00:19:06.930
This is it!

00:19:07.040 --> 00:19:08.940
Clippers.

00:19:09.640 --> 00:19:11.610
What?!

00:19:23.650 --> 00:19:26.310
I've got to stop
them!

00:19:50.580 --> 00:19:53.510
There goes my chance to get married!

00:19:53.510 --> 00:19:55.850
Quit whining! We're almost there!

00:19:56.820 --> 00:19:58.250
You're one
to talk!

00:19:58.350 --> 00:20:01.320
At least you've got someone
to marry!

00:20:02.620 --> 00:20:03.890
Do I?

00:20:03.890 --> 00:20:04.880
Huh?

00:20:05.060 --> 00:20:07.790
I don't know! I'm not
sure of anything!

00:20:11.170 --> 00:20:14.160
Red, he loves me. Blue,
he loves me not.

00:20:14.340 --> 00:20:15.800
Hey, what are
you doing?

00:20:18.440 --> 00:20:19.870
Miyuki!

00:20:48.470 --> 00:20:52.460
I don't know how I can
thank you enough.

00:20:52.570 --> 00:20:55.510
Thanks to you, nobody was hurt
and everything turned out fine.

00:20:55.680 --> 00:20:57.840
Well, it was really nothing
at all. Right, Miyuki?

00:20:58.010 --> 00:20:58.840
Mm-hmm.

00:20:59.010 --> 00:21:03.810
This is a little difficult for
me to bring up, but...

00:21:03.920 --> 00:21:10.220
...the merchandise you used earlier
amounts to this total right here.

00:21:11.660 --> 00:21:15.220
And the estimated cost of
repairing our clock...

00:21:15.330 --> 00:21:17.390
...amounts to this
much right here.

00:21:20.230 --> 00:21:25.430
But, seeing as the two of
you saved our store...

00:21:25.540 --> 00:21:28.510
...you will not be
charged for it.

00:21:29.610 --> 00:21:34.950
I'd also like for you to take home
the clothes you're wearing...

00:21:35.050 --> 00:21:37.810
...as a token of our
appreciation.

00:21:37.990 --> 00:21:39.950
Thank you very
much.

00:21:42.820 --> 00:21:44.990
Too bad we ripped them apart!

00:21:44.990 --> 00:21:45.830
What are you saying?!

00:21:45.830 --> 00:21:47.800
But, you know...

00:21:55.340 --> 00:22:00.840
<i>Every time I fall</i>
<i>out of love...</i>

00:22:04.850 --> 00:22:11.450
<i>... everything that I see</i>
<i>turns monochrome.</i>

00:22:12.050 --> 00:22:18.390
<i>We often used to go see the</i>
<i>games at the stadium...</i>

00:22:18.460 --> 00:22:28.470
<i>... but the good old days mean</i>
<i>nothing to me anymore.</i>

00:22:28.540 --> 00:22:42.480
<i>Even after you've gone, I still wanna</i>
<i>tell the world what it is that I love.</i>

00:22:42.780 --> 00:22:50.730
<i>Looking up to the sky, I try</i>
<i>holding back the tears.</i>

00:22:50.790 --> 00:22:59.300
<i>Flags were moving in the wind and</i>
<i>things seemed brighter yesterday.</i>

00:22:59.530 --> 00:23:07.340
<i>Looking up to the sky, we used</i>
<i>to talk about our dreams.</i>

00:23:07.440 --> 00:23:16.910
<i>No matter how far out of reach they seemed,</i>
<i>dreams could come true, or so it felt.</i>

00:23:17.320 --> 00:23:24.390
<i>Tell me that that fire in your</i>
<i>eyes was not a lie.</i>

00:23:26.460 --> 00:23:27.890
"For regularity..."

00:23:28.100 --> 00:23:29.590
What's lactobacillus?

00:23:29.760 --> 00:23:34.000
It's a germ that breaks down
lactose into lactic acid.

00:23:34.100 --> 00:23:35.760
It's also good for
your digestion!

00:23:35.940 --> 00:23:36.430
What's tuna?

00:23:36.600 --> 00:23:38.200
A species of marine fish belonging
to the family <i>scombridae.</i>

00:23:38.310 --> 00:23:41.400
Length is over 3 meters,
weight is 150-200 kg.

00:23:41.510 --> 00:23:44.170
The meat is dark red, and especially
tasty in the winter.

00:23:44.280 --> 00:23:46.340
Next time, You're Under
Arrest, File 31...

00:23:46.450 --> 00:23:48.020
..."The 40-Below Duel."

00:23:48.150 --> 00:23:50.150
Especially tasty in
the winter, huh?
